{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555694-totem-avatar-as-a-familiar","id":1555694,"title":"Totem Avatar as a Familiar.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-20T17:53:14-08:00","id":1555694,"title":"Totem Avatar as a Familiar.","content":"So, when an Incarna likes you they can send a Jaggling of themselves to you to be your spirit guide. But what about as a familiar? For instance, what if you wanted Easy Credit to give you a Jaggling of herself to help supervise your company, and thought it might be worthwhile for her to be material? Appropriate chiminage is made, perhaps you clear out a nest of Sabbat who were interfering with a business interest of hers and you do it in her name, and she becomes both your spirit animal AND your familiar at once. Does this seem too outrageous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T20:44:21-08:00","id":1555704,"title":"","content":"As long as the stats are within the premises of the background, no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> The ST may have to ponder how much this level of presence of an Incarna will affect the story, though, so this isn't necessarily ok in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> But outrageous? No, it isn't. Only the Garou may be pissed at the level of commitment this Totem has to the Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T20:53:17-08:00","id":1555706,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in the rules against it. Revised even did a fairly long sidebar on stacking these sorts of Backgrounds together with a basic &quot;if you ST is OK with it, and it fits your character, go for it, just remember that's a lot of eggs in one basket.&quot; Though keep in mind there is a Merit for having an Avatar that's a physically present character that your ST might require you to have on top of the Familiar Background. Familiars can also be things besides animals. Revised and M20 have rules that let you make a familiar that could be something like a smart phone with the Easy Credit app that manifests your Familiar's abilities in a fashion more in keeping with their spiritual nature (you could even stack Wonder on it and make it a Fetish!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T05:27:55-08:00","id":1555714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://postimg.cc/9wjqkFss\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://postimg.cc/9wjqkFss\" data-thumb-url=\"https://postimg.cc/9wjqkFss\" data-title=\"Click 